WEBVTT

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:05.930
Because we’re still doing okay,

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:12.390
we can become even stronger!

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:17.900
Aiming for the tall and wide sky,

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:21.450
I let go of what I was up until yesterday.

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:24.260
Those lies that were easily seen through and my tedious day-by-day life;

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:26.980
I left them both behind.

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:29.870
I narrowed my eyes at the new morning

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:33.280
Today we shall also venture out
to live our lives again.

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:36.720
Even the slight loneliness that sometimes comes about,

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:39.460
I consider important.

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:45.070
Even the truth I felt some day…

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:51.440
…is urging us to go on into the future.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:56.450
The world that we had all aimed for…

00:00:56.450 --> 00:01:03.470
We will arrive at it, no matter what our pasts are.

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:08.460
We continued forward, even if it is a steep path…

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:11.900
…because we’re still doing okay,

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:18.280
and we can become even stronger!

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:37.500
Yahoo!

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:39.370
We’re there! We’re there! We’re there!

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:42.370
The wind is so refreshing!

00:01:42.370 --> 00:01:45.540
So this is what a vacation at a summer resort feels like!

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:47.890
The wind is too strong.
Close the window.

00:01:47.890 --> 00:01:49.130
Eh, but…

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:55.840
CLOSE IT!

00:01:56.120 --> 00:01:57.340
O-Okay!

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:08.940
It seems weird somehow…

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:10.020
Weird, weird, weird!

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:11.900
Eh? What is it?

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:18.310
But, Onii-chan and the Ichijou sisters haven’t exchanged a single word since this morning!

00:02:18.770 --> 00:02:21.630
I have a suspicious feeling about this…

00:02:21.630 --> 00:02:23.230
It’s nothing!

00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:25.700
That’s because we’ve been feeling a bit sleepy since morning.

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:26.960
Yes, yes!

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:29.250
Just leave me alone!

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:39.880
He’s just nervous because he’s sitting next to a girl.

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:42.360
Okay, let’s trade seats.

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:45.260
Keisuke-kun, you get carsick unless you sit in front.

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:47.490
In addition, I want to arrive before noon.

00:02:47.490 --> 00:02:49.280
I’m going to speed up a bit.

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:52.400
Everyone, please fasten your seat belts!

00:02:54.350 --> 00:02:56.430
Mr. Truck, I’m going ahead!

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:03.030
Ah, excuse me.

00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:05.040
I’m sorry!

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:08.360
I’m sorry!

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:09.250
It’s okay.

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:11.940
I really envy you, Nozomu!

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:37.400
Miyabi-san, have we arrived?

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:38.940
It’s over there.

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:43.690
A chateau?

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:47.410
I believe that is the summer residence of the Sakurazuki family.

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:49.830
What?!

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:05.660
Sakurazuki Mountain Chateau?

00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:09.820
This is it. But it looks like we still have a long way to go.

00:04:20.930 --> 00:04:24.100
It’s incredible! It’s like we’re not in Japan anymore!

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:28.020
The Sakurazuki twins must be incredible ladies!

00:04:28.020 --> 00:04:30.200
It’s so surprising!

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:32.960
So all this is Sakurazuki land?

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:35.710
There’s someone to guide us.

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:39.210
Yeah! Without someone to guide us,
we’ll definitely get lost.

00:04:49.170 --> 00:04:50.060
I see it!

00:05:04.460 --> 00:05:05.450
Welcome!

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:07.660
We’ve been waiting for you!

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:08.730
Hey there.

00:05:08.730 --> 00:05:09.660
Hello!

00:05:10.490 --> 00:05:12.670
Welcome to the Sakurazuki Mountain chateau!

00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:15.470
Hey, Kira-chan, Yura-chan.

00:05:15.470 --> 00:05:16.630
Thank you for inviting us.

00:05:17.010 --> 00:05:18.110
Oh, it’s not much.

00:05:18.820 --> 00:05:20.370
And that must be…

00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:23.310
Ah, this is Miyabi-san. She’s taking care of me.

00:05:23.310 --> 00:05:24.630
I’m very pleased to meet you.

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:27.340
Thank you for inviting me as well.

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:29.280
Wow, she’s beautiful!

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:32.210
Thank you for taking care of Nozomu-kun.

00:05:32.210 --> 00:05:35.090
Ah, are these Ruru-chan and Rara-chan?

00:05:35.090 --> 00:05:36.210
They’re so cute!

00:05:36.210 --> 00:05:37.490
I’m Ruru!

00:05:37.490 --> 00:05:39.860
I’m Rara! And this is Billy!

00:05:40.510 --> 00:05:42.560
We met at the veterinary clinic last time, didn’t we?

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:44.720
He seems to be full of energy!

00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:49.010
There are three sets of twins here now.

00:05:49.010 --> 00:05:50.280
It seems so incredible!

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:53.070
So everyone, please come in.

00:05:53.070 --> 00:05:53.950
You too, Kosaka-kun.

00:05:54.910 --> 00:05:55.880
Yes!

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:04.590
Welcome.

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:07.010
We’re honored.

00:06:09.850 --> 00:06:11.290
Incredible!

00:06:11.290 --> 00:06:13.890
Ah, hello. Please take care of us.

00:06:14.530 --> 00:06:15.950
It’s beautiful!

00:06:15.950 --> 00:06:17.890
It’s like being a princess!

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:20.730
If you need anything,
don’t hesitate to ask.

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:24.730
Onee-chan, may we bring
Billy into the room?

00:06:24.730 --> 00:06:28.740
That’s fine. We’ll also have food prepared for him.

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:30.300
Yippee!

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:31.740
Ah, over here.

00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:33.040
Wow…

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:34.360
It’s so spacious!

00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:39.090
This is the Great Hall. Everyone’s rooms are on the top floor.

00:06:39.090 --> 00:06:40.750
We’ll take the elevator.

00:06:46.190 --> 00:06:47.050
We’re here!

00:06:47.050 --> 00:06:49.530
Wow! There are so many rooms!

00:06:49.530 --> 00:06:51.630
It seems like we could get lost!

00:06:51.630 --> 00:06:53.680
How many rooms are there?

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:55.470
Umm, I think…

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:56.400
Umm…

00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:57.580
So apparently…

00:06:57.580 --> 00:07:00.230
there are more than you can count?

00:07:00.740 --> 00:07:02.650
Y-yes.

00:07:04.370 --> 00:07:07.850
If you play hide-and-seek here,
it’d be impossible to find anyone.

00:07:07.850 --> 00:07:11.490
Yeah, maybe someone’s still hiding around here.

00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:16.850
Say, did you ever lose anyone in here while playing hide-and-seek?

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:23.480
We never had any friends to play with…

00:07:23.480 --> 00:07:25.790
and we’ve never played hide-and-seek.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:32.170
Wow, it’s an incredible room!

00:07:32.170 --> 00:07:33.930
It’s so incredible!

00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:35.600
It’s spacious and the ceiling is so high!

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:39.600
Incredible! It’s like a king’s throne!

00:07:40.480 --> 00:07:42.360
This is even more incredible!

00:07:42.360 --> 00:07:45.860
It’s like the garden at the Palace of Versailles! Not that I’ve been there…

00:07:45.860 --> 00:07:49.620
It seems like all we can say is “incredible”.

00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:51.410
But it really IS incredible!

00:07:51.410 --> 00:07:53.580
Maybe it’s a bit too much for us.

00:07:53.580 --> 00:07:56.860
No matter where you go…

00:07:58.970 --> 00:08:03.850
The more unattainable a goal, the more fired up I get!

00:08:03.850 --> 00:08:04.210
Huh?

00:08:04.610 --> 00:08:07.520
We’ll meet in the hall in ten minutes.

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:09.710
We’ll be playing in the nearby creek.

00:08:14.320 --> 00:08:16.180
Kira-chan and Yura-chan haven’t come yet?

00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:19.750
What? They’re the ones who called everyone down.

00:08:19.750 --> 00:08:21.140
Wow…

00:08:21.540 --> 00:08:23.320
What a big door!

00:08:26.690 --> 00:08:27.790
It won’t open!

00:08:27.790 --> 00:08:30.940
Oh, you can’t go into that room. Sorry.

00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:35.520
There’s a reason why we can’t allow people to enter. I’m sorry.

00:08:39.190 --> 00:08:41.140
But, Misses…

00:08:41.140 --> 00:08:42.850
It’s okay, Kenmochi-san.

00:08:42.850 --> 00:08:45.430
You don’t have to worry about us.

00:08:45.430 --> 00:08:46.290
We’ll be off!

00:08:47.770 --> 00:08:49.050
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:08:49.050 --> 00:08:50.420
Let’s take the shortest path!

00:08:51.020 --> 00:08:52.080
Bye Mama!

00:08:52.080 --> 00:08:53.430
We’re off!

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:55.430
Be careful!

00:08:56.030 --> 00:08:58.680
Onee-chan, how close is the creek?

00:08:59.240 --> 00:09:00.940
It’s a bit far.

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:04.440
But if we go through here, we can get there faster.

00:09:04.440 --> 00:09:08.560
When we were younger,
we often sneaked out to play.

00:09:08.560 --> 00:09:10.700
Of course, Kenmochi-san had to keep it secret.

00:09:10.700 --> 00:09:14.700
So, Kira-chan and Yura-chan did that kind of thing.

00:09:16.040 --> 00:09:17.700
This way!

00:09:24.010 --> 00:09:26.960
It seems that Kira-chan and Yura-chan are really active!

00:09:27.480 --> 00:09:32.230
When we return to this chateau, it’s like we’ve returned to our childhood.

00:09:32.230 --> 00:09:33.690
Right, Yura-chan?

00:09:33.690 --> 00:09:35.470
Yes, Kira-chan.

00:09:41.400 --> 00:09:43.260
You can’t do that!

00:09:43.260 --> 00:09:48.710
Ah… doing such things.
It’s really unrefined, Misses!

00:09:51.080 --> 00:09:53.040
I should have gone along with them.

00:09:53.040 --> 00:09:56.750
If it weren’t for the Master’s 86th trial:
“Go fishing on your own” –

00:09:56.750 --> 00:10:00.820
I would’ve gone along with them!

00:10:00.820 --> 00:10:04.790
You don’t have to be so flustered, Kenmochi-san.

00:10:04.790 --> 00:10:05.540
But…

00:10:06.050 --> 00:10:09.430
Kids grow up as they will,
even without supervision.

00:10:09.430 --> 00:10:12.670
Even though they may do this or that along the way…

00:10:12.670 --> 00:10:14.360
What are you saying?

00:10:14.360 --> 00:10:17.530
Do this… and that?!

00:10:24.840 --> 00:10:26.870
Why is it moving?

00:10:26.870 --> 00:10:28.390
Why?

00:10:28.390 --> 00:10:29.500
It’s coming. It’s coming.

00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:30.650
Pull back on the rod!

00:10:43.380 --> 00:10:44.790
That was fun!

00:10:44.790 --> 00:10:46.610
Let’s do it again, Yura-chan!

00:10:46.610 --> 00:10:48.330
Yes, Kira-chan!

00:10:48.330 --> 00:10:50.250
I’ll help you this time.

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:52.620
Let’s look over there!

00:10:52.620 --> 00:10:53.770
Okay!

00:10:59.870 --> 00:11:01.380
What kind of fish is it?

00:11:01.380 --> 00:11:03.570
I think it’s a char or a trout.

00:11:03.570 --> 00:11:06.640
Speaking of which – you hate fish, right?

00:11:07.290 --> 00:11:07.950
Eh?

00:11:07.950 --> 00:11:12.550
Umm, I’m okay with eating them, but touching them is…

00:11:12.550 --> 00:11:14.830
Nozomu-chan, you still remember!

00:11:14.830 --> 00:11:16.880
Yeah. When we were in preschool,

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:21.030
you were scared out of your wits when it was our turn to take care of the killifish.

00:11:21.030 --> 00:11:23.200
Even though it was just a killifish.

00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:27.590
You kept screaming every time we had to change its water.

00:11:27.590 --> 00:11:30.700
Yeah, you ended up doing everything in my stead.

00:11:30.700 --> 00:11:31.210
Yeah.

00:11:40.870 --> 00:11:43.090
Eh? A barbecue on the riverbank?

00:11:43.090 --> 00:11:46.100
Yes. It would be even tastier if everyone cooked together.

00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:53.080
We even caught quite a bit of fish. We should do fine with just more fish and vegetables.

00:11:53.670 --> 00:11:59.110
But the western-style formal dinner for the misses is already prepared.

00:11:59.110 --> 00:12:00.830
We’re sorry.

00:12:00.830 --> 00:12:05.690
We wanted to try out barbecuing, right, Kira-chan?

00:12:05.690 --> 00:12:07.160
Yes, Yura-chan.

00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:10.660
Therefore, please enjoy this dinner with the house staff.

00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:12.120
Yes, ma’ams.

00:12:13.290 --> 00:12:15.630
Now, let’s go shopping.

00:12:15.630 --> 00:12:18.840
Yay! Barbecue…

00:12:18.840 --> 00:12:20.530
Barbecue!

00:12:20.530 --> 00:12:22.100
Barbecue!

00:12:22.100 --> 00:12:23.800
Barbecue!

00:12:22.380 --> 00:12:24.510
Misses, your purse.

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:28.760
Don’t worry. They can use their own spending money.

00:12:29.060 --> 00:12:32.150
But, our Misses…

00:12:32.150 --> 00:12:35.940
They’re with Nozomu-kun and the others, so there’s no need to worry, okay?

00:12:35.940 --> 00:12:37.940
Okay…

00:12:38.650 --> 00:12:41.450
Therefore, let’s split up and find the things that are on the list.

00:12:41.450 --> 00:12:47.310
We only have about 5,000 yen,
so try to find the bargain buys.

00:12:47.310 --> 00:12:49.450
We have the necessary firewood in the chateau.

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:51.080
Got it. Now, begin!

00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:52.870
Yay!

00:13:05.400 --> 00:13:06.550
Kaoruko-chan!

00:13:07.600 --> 00:13:09.810
You should always eat your celery.

00:13:11.260 --> 00:13:12.640
You caught me.

00:13:13.480 --> 00:13:16.690
So you remember that I hate celery, Nozomu-chan?

00:13:16.690 --> 00:13:22.320
Yeah, I used to eat the celery in your lunch all the time.

00:13:22.320 --> 00:13:25.410
Back then, you seemed like a hero.

00:13:25.860 --> 00:13:27.370
Eh? Really?

00:13:42.630 --> 00:13:45.600
Here you go, Nozomu-oniichan. The meat is done!

00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:46.180
Thank you.

00:13:46.550 --> 00:13:47.730
Me too…

00:13:47.730 --> 00:13:50.460
Here you go. Keisuke-kun should have some vegetables.

00:13:50.460 --> 00:13:52.810
A whole green onion?!

00:13:59.260 --> 00:14:00.110
That’s dangerous!

00:14:00.680 --> 00:14:02.560
Don’t get burnt!

00:14:02.560 --> 00:14:08.580
It’s okay as long as Kira-san and Yura-san are having fun, right?

00:14:16.020 --> 00:14:19.290
It’s the first time I’ve eaten such a delicious dinner!

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:20.780
Right, Yura-chan?

00:14:20.780 --> 00:14:22.750
Yes, Kira-chan.

00:14:23.100 --> 00:14:25.810
That’s a relief, right, Keisuke?

00:14:25.810 --> 00:14:29.900
Yeah. If you want to do this again, you can ask me anytime.

00:14:29.900 --> 00:14:30.970
Sure.

00:14:32.720 --> 00:14:34.820
The day’s already over.

00:14:34.820 --> 00:14:36.740
It’s a pity.

00:14:36.740 --> 00:14:41.230
Hey, it’s a bit early to go to sleep.
Why don’t we play hide-and-seek?

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:43.110
Hide-and-seek?

00:14:43.110 --> 00:14:46.850
Eh? Why do we have to play a kids’ game?

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:53.580
Ah, is that so? It’s okay.

00:14:54.090 --> 00:14:58.410
If we restrict ourselves to this hall,
we shouldn’t get lost.

00:14:58.410 --> 00:15:00.000
It seems interesting!

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:01.200
Let’s play!

00:15:01.200 --> 00:15:02.050
Let’s play hide-and-seek!

00:15:03.670 --> 00:15:04.550
Okay.

00:15:04.970 --> 00:15:07.210
Jankenpon!

00:15:04.970 --> 00:15:07.210
Jankenpon = Rock, paper, scissors

00:15:07.210 --> 00:15:09.410
Okay, Nozomu… you’re it.

00:15:12.380 --> 00:15:19.690
1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6…

00:15:20.690 --> 00:15:22.780
29, 30!

00:15:23.250 --> 00:15:24.280
Okay, let’s go!

00:15:34.670 --> 00:15:36.670
Nozomu-kun, over here!

00:15:36.670 --> 00:15:38.570
Kira-chan, that’s not how you play…

00:15:38.570 --> 00:15:42.630
Oh yeah! If we’re found, we’re it.

00:15:42.630 --> 00:15:43.580
Yeah, but…

00:15:49.200 --> 00:15:51.000
He missed us.

00:15:59.210 --> 00:16:00.510
I found you, Keisuke!

00:16:00.510 --> 00:16:01.650
Eh! That was fast!

00:16:02.230 --> 00:16:06.060
Your hiding places haven’t changed very much since preschool.

00:16:10.140 --> 00:16:11.400
Gotcha!

00:16:13.530 --> 00:16:14.510
Ehhh!

00:16:24.020 --> 00:16:26.960
They got really tired today. We’ll just let them sleep.

00:16:27.880 --> 00:16:31.260
He’s pretty cute when he sleeps.

00:16:37.510 --> 00:16:39.100
And he manages to do this.

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:48.270
Ah, I found Kira-chan and Yura-chan!

00:16:49.580 --> 00:16:51.280
We were found!

00:16:51.750 --> 00:16:54.250
Okay, next round! Let’s go!

00:16:54.250 --> 00:16:59.120
1, 2, 3, 4, 5…

00:17:00.730 --> 00:17:01.910
This is no good.

00:17:02.920 --> 00:17:04.410
This place is too obvious.

00:17:18.850 --> 00:17:20.680
It’s okay to enter.

00:17:22.540 --> 00:17:24.410
It’s okay if it’s you, Nozomu-kun.

00:17:24.410 --> 00:17:27.690
Let’s go in. We want you to take a look.

00:17:31.620 --> 00:17:32.690
Come in.

00:17:55.090 --> 00:17:58.550
This was our mother’s room.

00:17:59.760 --> 00:18:00.840
“Was”?

00:18:00.840 --> 00:18:04.770
She died from an illness
when we were five.

00:18:05.850 --> 00:18:06.770
Just like mine…

00:18:08.970 --> 00:18:13.430
We have never allowed anyone
to enter this room other than Papa.

00:18:13.430 --> 00:18:17.110
No one else, not even Kenmochi-san, has ever entered here.

00:18:17.110 --> 00:18:20.780
Only special people can enter this room.

00:18:20.780 --> 00:18:23.750
Eh? But someone like me…

00:18:24.140 --> 00:18:25.450
No.

00:18:25.450 --> 00:18:30.570
We have been paying attention to you, Nozomu-kun, and we have these feelings…

00:18:30.570 --> 00:18:33.670
We didn’t understand what they were.

00:18:33.670 --> 00:18:36.990
We wondered why our hearts would often beat rapidly.

00:18:36.990 --> 00:18:40.400
We didn’t understand these feelings very well.

00:18:40.400 --> 00:18:44.670
Why would it always happen when we were talking to you?

00:18:47.910 --> 00:18:53.400
We finally realized it when you suggested playing hide-and-seek together.

00:18:54.620 --> 00:18:57.530
Why don’t we play hide-and-seek?

00:18:59.570 --> 00:19:03.120
This is the feeling of “love”.

00:19:03.120 --> 00:19:04.620
We thought of this together.

00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:09.210
It’s the first time we’ve liked a guy…

00:19:09.210 --> 00:19:14.120
Umm, ummm…
we don’t know what to do!

00:19:14.630 --> 00:19:16.460
But… but…

00:19:16.460 --> 00:19:18.880
We wanted to tell you about our feelings.

00:19:25.370 --> 00:19:28.730
Can we both fall in love with you?

00:19:34.360 --> 00:19:36.390
This is strange.

00:19:36.390 --> 00:19:38.570
Nozomu-chan appears
to have disappeared.

00:19:39.430 --> 00:19:40.320
We need to leave.

00:19:40.670 --> 00:19:43.060
Nozomu-kun, umm…

00:19:43.540 --> 00:19:45.190
Are you…

00:19:45.190 --> 00:19:48.130
going out with the Ichijou sisters?

00:19:48.130 --> 00:19:49.210
No… No, I’m not.

00:19:50.110 --> 00:19:51.350
I’m relieved!

00:19:51.350 --> 00:19:52.710
He isn’t going out with anyone!

00:19:52.710 --> 00:19:53.800
No, that’s not…

00:19:55.030 --> 00:19:57.700
It’s okay if you don’t answer us now.

00:19:57.700 --> 00:20:00.510
We will wait. Therefore…

00:20:02.630 --> 00:20:05.020
Maybe he went back
to his room. I’ll go look.

00:20:06.200 --> 00:20:08.710
We have another favor to ask.

00:20:10.610 --> 00:20:11.150
Come on.

00:20:23.620 --> 00:20:24.670
Well?

00:20:24.670 --> 00:20:26.240
Did you find him?

00:20:26.240 --> 00:20:27.160
No.

00:20:27.810 --> 00:20:29.790
Where in the world could he be hiding?

00:20:32.990 --> 00:20:34.750
It’s okay, just take it slowly.

00:20:34.750 --> 00:20:36.980
We’re fine.

00:20:36.980 --> 00:20:38.160
It’s okay.

00:20:47.010 --> 00:20:48.930
We finally did it, Yura-chan!

00:20:49.480 --> 00:20:53.100
Yeah! We always wanted to do this when we were little.

00:20:53.100 --> 00:20:54.810
To watch the stars from here…

00:21:03.730 --> 00:21:07.490
All the things we’ve done here were all thanks to you, Nozomu-kun.

00:21:07.490 --> 00:21:10.400
Yes, all thanks to Nozomu-kun.

00:21:10.400 --> 00:21:13.690
I think there will be lots of happy things starting from today.

00:21:13.690 --> 00:21:17.080
Yes, definitely. If Nozomu-kun is with us…

00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:58.000
dokomademo tsuzuku sora

00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:58.000
Oh, the sky that continues no matter where you go…

00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:04.050
daisuki na kono machi de

00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:04.050
In this town that I love…

00:22:04.050 --> 00:22:10.050
takusan no omoide to, hora,

00:22:04.050 --> 00:22:10.050
With all our memories, now look!

00:22:10.050 --> 00:22:16.020
onaji dake hohoende

00:22:10.050 --> 00:22:16.020
We are smiling the same way

00:22:16.020 --> 00:22:26.700
itsudemo kimi no tonari ni iyoutoshiteru no wa

00:22:16.020 --> 00:22:26.700
To always be trying to be besides you…

00:22:26.700 --> 00:22:39.020
mukashi kara no kuse datte omotteru kedo

00:22:26.700 --> 00:22:39.020
…is, I believe, a bad habit I’ve had for a long time

00:22:39.020 --> 00:22:45.140
“mata ashita” tte te wo furu toki ni wa

00:22:39.020 --> 00:22:45.140
When we wave our hands saying “see you tomorrow,”

00:22:45.140 --> 00:22:50.930
sukoshi dake samishii kigasuru yo

00:22:45.140 --> 00:22:50.930
I realize that I’m feeling a little lonely at that moment

00:22:50.930 --> 00:22:57.230
tooku naru kimi no senaka mitsumete

00:22:50.930 --> 00:22:57.230
Staring at your back that is getting further away,

00:22:57.230 --> 00:23:03.190
nandaka, fushigi na kimochi

00:22:57.230 --> 00:23:03.190
For some reason, a mysterious feeling…

00:23:03.190 --> 00:23:09.090
kono mune ni hirogatte yuku

00:23:03.190 --> 00:23:09.090
…is spreading through this heart of mine

00:23:11.700 --> 00:23:12.700
This is Kaoruko!

00:23:12.700 --> 00:23:13.820
This is Sumireko!

00:23:13.820 --> 00:23:17.540
Hey, I heard that an unknown girl appeared at Sourin Temple.

00:23:17.540 --> 00:23:20.960
Yeah, it seems she’s really good at drawing.

00:23:20.970 --> 00:23:23.530
Next time: The White Sketchbook!
